From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: take the CRTC's encoder from the atomic state

dpu_crtc_get_vblank_counter() and dpu_crtc_get_scanout_position() find the
encoder through the legacy encoder->crtc link. drm_atomic_helper_
update_legacy_modeset_state() clears that link and rebuilds it on every
atomic commit that carries the connector (wlroots puts CRTC_ID on the
connector in each commit), and it stays NULL while the CRTC is switched
off. A vblank counter or timestamp query that lands in that window logs
'*ERROR* no encoder found for crtc 0' (r121 Phosh session: six of them
around blank/unblank, dmesg 01:20-01:39) and, because dpu_kms sets
max_vblank_count = 0xffffffff, feeds a counter value of 0 into
drm_update_vblank_count(), which jumps the vblank sequence userspace sees.

Use the encoder mask of the CRTC's atomic state first; fall back to the
legacy link (dpu_crtc_disable() runs after the state swap with an empty new
mask). A query on a CRTC that is really off is not an error: report it at
debug level and keep returning 0/false.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -56,6 +56,19 @@
 	struct drm_device *dev = crtc->dev;
 	struct drm_encoder *encoder;
 
+	/*
+	 * The legacy encoder->crtc link is torn down and rebuilt by
+	 * drm_atomic_helper_update_legacy_modeset_state() on every commit that
+	 * carries the connector, and it is NULL for a CRTC that is switched
+	 * off. The atomic CRTC state is what actually drives the encoder, so
+	 * take the encoder from its mask first and use the legacy link only as
+	 * a fallback (dpu_crtc_disable() after the state swap).
+	 */
+	if (crtc->state) {
+		drm_for_each_encoder_mask(encoder, dev, crtc->state->encoder_mask)
+			return encoder;
+	}
+
 	drm_for_each_encoder(encoder, dev)
 		if (encoder->crtc == crtc)
 			return encoder;
@@ -189,7 +202,8 @@
 {
 	struct drm_encoder *encoder = get_encoder_from_crtc(crtc);
 	if (!encoder) {
-		DRM_ERROR("no encoder found for crtc %d\n", crtc->index);
+		/* Vblank query on a CRTC that is off: nothing to count. */
+		DRM_DEBUG_KMS("no encoder found for crtc %d\n", crtc->index);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
@@ -279,7 +293,7 @@
 
 	encoder = get_encoder_from_crtc(crtc);
 	if (!encoder) {
-		DRM_ERROR("no encoder found for crtc %d\n", pipe);
+		DRM_DEBUG_KMS("no encoder found for crtc %d\n", pipe);
 		return false;
 	}
 
